9 [math.NT], 2024.\n\nEXAMPLE\n\nFor n=3, the a(3) = 3 pairs are (5,6), (6,6), (6,5).\n\nFor n=4, the a(4) = 10 pairs are (u,10), (u,9), (10,8), (10,7), where 7 <= u <= 10.\n\nCROSSREFS\n\nSequence in context: A088809 A364534 A069229 * A316587 A309300 A271357\n\nAdjacent sequences: A378620 A378621 A378622 * A378624 A378625 A378626\n\nKEYWORD\n\nnonn,more,hard\n\nAUTHOR\n\nKevin O'Bryant, Dec 02 2024\n\nSTATUS\n\napproved--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHePhySTO – HEidelberg PHYsics Seminar Talks Organizer (https://www.physik.uni-heidelberg.de/hephysto/index.php?id=12627&s=talk)\nciteturn9search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; [https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21194](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21194) David Conlon, Jacob Fox, Huy Tuan Pham, Liana Yepremyan ... 26 May 2026, 13:00 ... Disproof of the Odd Hadwiger Conjecture\n\n### On the clique number of random Cayley graphs and related topics\n\nJohn Larkin Image\n\n[https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21194](https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21194) David Conlon, Jacob Fox, Huy Tuan Pham, Liana Yepremyan\n\nDiscrete Mathematics Reading Group\n26 May 2026, 13:00\nLocation not specified.\nAdd to calendar\n\n\nUpcoming:\n\nDisproof of the Odd Hadwiger Conjecture\nCynthia Xie\nTue, 16 Jun 2026, 13:00\nUncovering biophysical mechanisms in morphogenesis\nJulia Eckert\nTue, 16 Jun 2026, 16:00\nLandau-Zener Spektroskopie of atomic tunneling systems\nArpan Gauai\nTue, 16 Jun 2026, 16:00\nUsing proof assistants as more than checkers, and how to write papers about it\nYannick Forster\nTue, 16 Jun 2026, 16:15\nSolving Inverse Problems in Astronomy with Invertible Neural Networks\nVictor Ksoll\nTue, 16 Jun 2026, 16:30--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:O'Bryant_K in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AO%27Bryant_K+in%3Amath)\nciteturn9search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Oct 28 2026 math.CO arXiv:2610.36207v1 ...   * Visualizing the Sum-Product Conjecture ... Nov 14 2024 math.NT math.CO arXiv:2411.08139v2\n\n  * Visualizing the Sum-Product Conjecture\n\nKevin O'Bryant\n\nNov 14 2024 math.NT math.CO arXiv:2411.08139v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2411.08139, author = {Kevin O'Bryant}, title = {{V}isualizing the {S}um-{P}roduct {C}onjecture}, year = {2024}, eprint = {2411.08139}, note = {arXiv:2411.08139v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nLet $SPP(n)$ be the set $\\left\\{\\big(|A+A|,|A A|\\big) : A\\subseteq {\\mathbb N}, |A|=n\\right\\}$ of sum-product pairs, where $A+A$ is the sumset $\\{a+b : a,b\\in A\\}$ and $A A$ is the product set $\\{ab:a,b\\in A\\}$. We construct a dataset consisting of 1162868 sets whose sum-product pairs are at least $84\\%$ of $SPP(n)$ for each $n\\le 32$. Notably, we do **not** see evidence in favor of Erdős's Sum-Product Conjecture in our dataset. For $n\\le 6$, we prove the exact value of $SPP(n)$. We include a number of conjectures, open problems, and observations motivated by this dataset, a large number of color visualizations.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHE SUM-PRODUCT PROBLEM FOR SMALL SETS II (https://alexricemath.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/SP2025paper.pdf)\nciteturn9search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Freiman, Foundations of a Structural Theory of Set Addition, Translations of Mathematical Monographs vol. ... 294 (2016), no. ... O’Bryant, Visualizing the sum-product conjecture, preprint (2024), arXiv:2411.08139.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Frobenius automorphism \\(\\sigma\\) acting on divisors by the rule (https://people.math.ethz.ch/~kowalski/jacobian-graphs.pdf)\nciteturn9search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; [6] D. ... Preprint https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.21194. ... Deligne, *La conjecture de Weil. ... Number Theory **10** (2024), no.\n------